      "writtenOn": "2020-11-30T21:01:46Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The register reserves bits [7:0] and bits [15:14].  This routine should ensure these bits are not set before writing the register.  \n\nIf bits 7:0 are set, it probably makes sense to round up by 256mA and always clear bit 7:0 before writing.\n\nThe DCProcHot limit is 12.8A (0x3200), so limiting to this value will ensure bits 15:14 are not written.",
